    "narrative": "The offensive core for LawDog today centers on **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest efficiency score at 73.64. Matching up against Tatsuya Imai (5.12 xERA), **Lawrence Butler** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the favorable opposing arm and a 13% platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for power and counting stats. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a must-start at 68.91; while facing a tougher arm in Jack Leiter, the combination of his elite talent and the elevated scoring floor provided by his placement in the #2 hole ensures he remains our most bankable asset. **Will Smith** and **Geraldo Perdomo** also grade out as strong plays, both projected to exploit high xERA matchups to bolster our production in a slate where avoiding stagnation is key.\n\nThe most challenging decision for the optimizer involved **Gleyber Torres**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 49.17. While **Gleyber Torres** garnered significant value from his projected leadoff spot and favorable wind conditions, the model favored the higher individual scoring thresholds of **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Bryson Stott**. **Bryson Stott**, in particular, holds a narrow edge due to the potential for stolen bases against a slower-to-deliver pitching staff, a critical factor given our strategic emphasis on SB efficiency. We are closely monitoring the lineups for **Will Smith**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Luis Arraez**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Taylor Ward**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Bryson Stott**; if any of these pieces move down in the order, their daily efficiency score will be subject to immediate downward revision. \n\nFinally, caution is advised regarding **Tyler Freeman**, who faces a daunting matchup against the talented Jacob Misiorowski (2.70 xERA). Although **Tyler Freeman** receives a modest score, the 19% penalty for facing such a high-c